{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfck8qjsveno5caygjVqT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The code in the diff supports the claim. `GetRecord` caches every error from `c.get` for `errorCacheTTL` (5 minutes). It makes no distinction between a `ReplyError` and a connect error, a timeout, or a cancelled context. `fetchFromServer` already separates those cases with `isErrorReply`, but `GetRecord` doesn't use that check when caching. The comment says \"Some records are permanently forbidden\", which points to caching only the permanent errors.\n\nA brief outage, a 1s timeout, or one cancelled context therefore blocks lookups of that key for 5 minutes. `loadMetadata` discards the error, so the item is tracked with no owner. Nothing is retried in that window, and the PR contains no code that would clear the cache early.\n\nThis is a real defect, but its impact is bounded. The cost is degraded metadata for a limited time, not data loss."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8597,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8597},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd75bbc0-31e3-44dc-b12d-966943cb7adc","uuid":"4d26bdb3-b438-41f7-bcc4-384c82be6654","timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:01:57.403Z","request_id":"req_011Cfck8q9AHXSbMKoiiUvpB"}
